<section class="section section-features" id="features">
  <div class="section-header center">
    <span class="eyebrow">What ships today</span>
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <p class="lead">General Folders gives companies a governed way to exchange operational data with customers and partners.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid card-grid-2">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <span class="feature-kicker">01</span>
      <h3>Run every transfer from one dashboard</h3>
      <p class="muted">Define an exchange, connect the source and destination endpoints you own, and set a cadence. General Folders schedules each run and reports live status.</p>
      <pre class="feature-ascii" aria-hidden="true">source ─▶ ▣ ─▶ dest
cadence · daily
status  · ● live</pre>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <span class="feature-kicker">02</span>
      <h3>Owned connections, isolated execution</h3>
      <p class="muted">Each organization connects only the endpoints it owns, with credentials held as secret references. Transfers execute in isolated workers, so payloads move through the run instead of pooling in storage.</p>
      <pre class="feature-ascii" aria-hidden="true">[key] secret refs
  └─ isolated worker
       src ╌╌▶ dst</pre>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <span class="feature-kicker">03</span>
      <h3>Proof every transfer worked</h3>
      <p class="muted">Every run records counts, checksums, retries, and failure detail behind a permission-scoped audit trail, so you can confirm delivery and troubleshoot without exposing raw data.</p>
      <pre class="feature-ascii" aria-hidden="true">status   · ✓ success
records  · verified
checksum · matched</pre>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <span class="feature-kicker">04</span>
      <h3>API-first, built to embed</h3>
      <p class="muted">Every exchange is an API object with status webhooks. Create and track transfers from the API, or embed the setup flow so your customers never leave your product.</p>
      <pre class="feature-ascii" aria-hidden="true">POST /v1/exchanges
  { src, dst, ... }
  ⇒ 201 · webhook ▸</pre>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

